    {
      "id": "p0211-b018",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This dialogue contains two main points of interest. First, astute players will realize that the \"old lady\" in Sans' story is actually Torie!, although the two have yet to meet in person.",
        "raw": "This dialogue contains two main points of interest. First, astute players will\nrealize that the \"old lady\" in Sans' story is actually Torie!, although the two\nhave yet to meet in person.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09111509,
          0.55717143,
          0.66943176,
          0.60565714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08873879,
          0.55645714,
          0.69976266,
          0.60672857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          32,
          33,
          34
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "这段对话有两个看点。首先，细心的玩家会意识到，Sans 故事里的“老太太”其实是 Toriel，尽管两人还没真正见过面。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09111509,
          0.55574286,
          0.69772292,
          0.60922857
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "justify",
        "auto_height": true,
        "limit_bottom": 0.6132857128571428,
        "snap_to_guides": true,
        "resize_anchor": "left"
      },
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09111509,
          0.55574286,
          0.69772292,
          0.60922857
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 29.0
      },
      "review_issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0211-b019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Second, and more importantly, Toriel's knock-knock joke plays with how the phrase \"old lady who\" sounds like the shout that yodelers make, \"yodel-ay-ee-oo\". But again, because knock-knock jokes don't exist in Japanese, and because this joke plays with English pronunciation, a literal translation of the scene would lose all meaning.",
        "raw": "Second, and more importantly,\nToriel's knock-knock joke plays\nwith how the phrase \"old lady who\"\nsounds like the shout that yodelers\nmake, \"yodel-ay-ee-oo\". But again,\nbecause knock-knock jokes don't exist\nin Japanese, and because this joke\nplays with English pronunciation, a\nliteral translation of the scene would\nlose all meaning.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09160463,
          0.62042857,
          0.38492912,
          0.79879286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08873879,
          0.61971429,
          0.38625495,
          0.79986429
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          35,
          38,
          40,
          42,
          44,
          46,
          48,
          50,
          51,
          52
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "其次，更重要的是，Toriel 的敲门笑话利用了“old lady who”听起来像约德尔唱法中的“yodel-ay-ee-oo”。但日本没有敲门笑话，笑点又依赖英语发音，因此直译会完全失去意义。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09077853,
          0.619,
          0.38492912,
