    {
      "id": "p0211-b021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "To get around these linguistic and cultural barriers, the translator replaced the English knock-knock joke with a pun on the Japanese word toku, which can mean both \"far away\" and \"talk\". The result is a cheesy joke in Japanese that perfectly matches Toriel's character.",
        "raw": "To get around these linguistic and cultural barriers, the translator replaced the\nEnglish knock-knock joke with a pun on the Japanese word toku, which can\nmean both \"far away\" and \"talk\". The result is a cheesy joke in Japanese that\nperfectly matches Toriel's character.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09208396,
          0.81324286,
          0.69569338,
          0.88157857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08873879,
          0.81252857,
          0.69976266,
          0.88265
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          53,
          54,
          55,
          56
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "为了绕过语言和文化障碍，译者把英语敲门笑话换成日语 tōku 的双关：它既可指“远”，也可指“聊天”（英语 talk 的借词）。这个日语冷笑话与 Toriel 的性格非常贴合。",
        "status": "draft",
